    {
     "id": "69b225a9-2e89-43f9-be16-831172bed375",
     "prompt": "Rewrite $x^2+6x+2$ in completed square form.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$(x+3)^2-7$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x+3)^2+2$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x+6)^2-34$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x-3)^2-7$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Halve 6 to get 3. Since $(x+3)^2=x^2+6x+9$, subtract 7 to obtain $(x+3)^2-7$."
    },
    {
     "id": "3a38a028-7405-4d27-9f03-e3e05e49f559",
     "prompt": "Complete the square for $x^2-5x+1$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$(x-\\frac{5}{2})^2-\\frac{3}{2}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x+\\frac{5}{2})^2-\\frac{21}{4}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x-\\frac{5}{2})^2-\\frac{21}{4}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$(x-\\frac{5}{2})^2+\\frac{21}{4}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Halve $-5$ to get $-\\frac{5}{2}$. Expanding the square produces an extra $\\frac{25}{4}$, so the correction gives $(x-\\frac{5}{2})^2-\\frac{21}{4}$."
    },
    {
     "id": "c4d6ca06-6fad-452f-ae54-42bc4dd2e5e9",
     "prompt": "Rewrite $3x^2-12x+7$ in the form $a(x+b)^2+c$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$3(x-2)^2+7$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$3(x+2)^2-5$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$3(x-4)^2-41$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$3(x-2)^2-5$",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Factor out 3 from the quadratic terms: $3(x^2-4x)+7$. Since $x^2-4x=(x-2)^2-4$, the expression becomes $3(x-2)^2-5$."
    },
    {
     "id": "9065b104-1216-4443-a692-162298d06ad4",
     "prompt": "Solve $x^2+8x+10=0$ exactly by completing the square.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$x=4\\pm\\sqrt{6}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=-4\\pm\\sqrt{6}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=-4\\pm\\sqrt{26}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=-4+\\sqrt{6}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Completing the square gives $(x+4)^2-6=0$, so $(x+4)^2=6$. Taking both square roots gives $x=-4\\pm\\sqrt{6}$."
    },
    {
     "id": "1671ad7c-afe0-4c48-9388-1fdec9ace765",
     "prompt": "What is the turning point of $y=(x+5)^2-2$?",
